policy_context: "A synthetic MSK policy with four independently gated reviews of one clinical snapshot. Determine which services apply from documented requests, treatment plans, and referrals in the clinical record; do not assume all four are requested. Fracture and degenerative-joint indication criteria follow the supplied guideline. Rehabilitation and recovery-support planning use explicitly synthetic rules inspired by its recovery sections. Branches share Approved and Needs review outcomes. Both may be reached for different requested services; select a reasoning trace to identify the service. There is no combined discharge decision. Degenerative and rehabilitation checks advance through consecutive Yes stages. Home support can fall back to a facility plan. A completed support plan does not authorize discharge. Batches reveal evidence about the same snapshot; answers never change."

